LibreSperidlabsIrisZ includes code ported from the Speridlabs Iris-Z SDK:

Source: https://github.com/speridlabs/iris-z-sdk (commit 6c8925f42a2a3581127609d771aa5bfece557467)
License: Apache-2.0.
Copyright 2026 SperidLabs (https://speridlabs.com).

The SDK's transformer, autoencoder, text-encoder and schedule code
(iris_z/model/) is from FLUX.2 by Black Forest Labs:

Source: https://github.com/black-forest-labs/flux2
License: Apache-2.0.
Copyright Black Forest Labs.

Iris-Z adds a modality embedding and per-grid noise levels to the FLUX.2
transformer (iris_z/model/model.py); the RGB-D samplers, depth decoding,
resolution choice and seed ensembling are the SDK's own (iris_z/rgbd.py,
iris_z/depth.py, iris_z/pipeline.py).

The port covers inference: the transformer forward pass Iris-Z samples with
(nn.py), the text-to-image and image-to-depth samplers, the schedule and the
depth decoding (pipeline.py), and the prompt embedders (text.py). Parameter
names mirror upstream so the released safetensors load with strict=True.
Changes from upstream: the reference-image KV-cache paths of the FLUX.2
transformer, which Iris-Z does not use, are left out, so attention is one
scaled_dot_product_attention over the text and image tokens (numerically the
same as upstream's attention with no reference tokens); the FLUX.2 VAE runs
through diffusers' AutoencoderKLFlux2 (Apache-2.0) with upstream's posterior
mean, 2x2 patchify and batch-norm normalization, loaded from the bfloat16
copy in FLUX.2-klein-4B and upcast to float32 (upstream reads float32
weights from the gated FLUX.2-dev repository); the text encoders keep only
the embedding path (no prompt upsampling, no content filters, which Iris-Z
does not call), and Qwen3's unquantized layers load in float32 explicitly,
as transformers 4.57 did by default; latent grids are reshaped instead of
scattered by position id, which gives the same tensors for Iris-Z's
row-major grids.

Weights are not redistributed by LibreYOLO. They download from their
publishers at pinned revisions: speridlabs/iris-z (FLUX Non-Commercial
License), the FLUX.2 VAE from black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4B
(Apache-2.0), mistralai/Mistral-Small-3.2-24B-Instruct-2506 with the
Mistral-Small-3.1-24B-Instruct-2503 processor (Apache-2.0), and
Qwen/Qwen3-8B-FP8 (Apache-2.0).

Iris-Z: https://speridlabs.com/research/iris-z
Paper: https://speridlabs.com/assets/research/iris-z/iris-z.pdf
